{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1785993952795057001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"core-elk-kin","assignee":"","attestations":{"plan-review":{"algorithm":"HMAC-SHA256","author":"Joe Oakhart","head_sha":"78a358d51aad34cd14a73c65b58e46375978ea85","key_id":"412fa5372ad877e0","kind":"plan-review","manifest":["plan-review: PASS","ticket: 8840-011f-5b6d-41ab","material: d132783a179bd0b5","model: claude-sonnet-4-6","runner: pydantic_ai","blocking: 0","advisory: 9","regver: bb57585159a067c5","verified-at-sha:4bd06245d66b0326f2bb8b86565ef0539db4d556","dep 223ed221bc5c4996e19c65e16d9aa393c29c6eafa0c8668451ae8382044f3055 src/rebar/_commands/transition.py","dep 1f571c88d575ada3f16f3725e769d80db64f463b5c93d4a59d02fbd32a945f7c src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest.py","dep 3cc1425059506b2ee0e8454047f5c625061aa4308d3fe7ff277b2b95768ae72a src/rebar/signing.py"],"signature":"27a0074fd9f39965e9522e600a40a0850c7e9f16e703ff19b4c73db487b3eaca","signed_at":1783126588366695000}},"author":"Joe Oakhart","authorship":{"signed":0,"unsigned":10},"authorship_ledger":[],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1783123873594901001,"creation_channel":"unknown","deps":[],"description":"## Why\n\nAttestation manifests must carry the rebar gate-code version+SHA for audit\nprovenance (epic jira-reb-596). This story adds the value where it is signed and\nthe parser to read it back — the core of the feature, with no build or display\nsurface yet.\n\n## What\n\n- Add a gate-code SHA/version resolver in `src/rebar/signing.py` (co-located with\n  and reusing the `head_sha()` idiom, line 337 — a `git -C … rev-parse` subprocess;\n  do NOT invent a new git wrapper). It returns `\"<version> (<short-sha>[-dirty])\"`,\n  or just `\"<version>\"` when no SHA is resolvable:\n  - Version: `rebar.__version__`.\n  - SHA: `git -C <dir of rebar.__file__> rev-parse --short HEAD` — the **rebar\n    source (gate code)** dir, NOT the target repo. Resolution is **live-git-first,\n    omit-last** (build-baked fallback = story 2).\n  - `-dirty` rule: append `-dirty` iff `git -C <dir of rebar.__file__> status\n    --porcelain` is non-empty (any staged / modified-tracked / untracked change in\n    the rebar source tree).\n  - Any git failure -> omit the SHA (version only) and emit a debug log\n    (silent-failure guard).\n- Append one `rebar-version:` line to BOTH manifests:\n  - `build_manifest` — `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest.py` (plan-review).\n  - `_verdict_manifest` — `src/rebar/_commands/transition.py:282`\n    (completion-verifier).\n- Add `manifest_rebar_version(manifest)` in `attest.py` (mirroring\n  `manifest_regver`) returning the stamp, or `None` for pre-stamp manifests.\n- `compute_validity` stays untouched and must never read the stamp.\n\n## Scope\n\nSigning + parsing only. Build-time baking = story 2; `show`/`verify_signature`\nsurfacing = story 3.\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `build_manifest` and `_verdict_manifest` each emit exactly one `rebar-version:` line in their output.\n- [ ] The resolver returns the live-git short SHA with a `-dirty` suffix when the rebar source checkout is dirty.\n- [ ] The resolver returns a version-only string (SHA omitted) and emits a debug log when git is unavailable / the install is non-git.\n- [ ] `manifest_rebar_version()` returns the stamp for a stamped manifest and `None` for a pre-stamp manifest.\n- [ ] `compute_validity` output is byte-for-byte unchanged, and a pre-stamp manifest still validates (proven by a passing test).\n- [ ] Existing tests asserting on `build_manifest` / `_verdict_manifest` output pass after being updated for the new line.\n- [ ] All of the following unit tests exist and pass: both-manifests-carry-line, live-checkout-dirty-resolution, git-absent-omit, parser-round-trip, pre-stamp-None.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/signing.py","reason":"add gate_code_version resolver (live-git SHA + dirty)"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest.py","reason":"emit rebar-version line in build_manifest + manifest_rebar_version parser"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/transition.py","reason":"emit rebar-version line in _verdict_manifest"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["parent","jira-reb-596"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"jira-reb-596","parent_status_uuid":"1886a46f-d76a-4310-9623-d14bc5575783","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"8840-011f-5b6d-41ab","ticket_type":"story","title":"Stamp gate-code version+SHA into attestation manifests + parser","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["b37b78e6-115d-49cf-8331-4b218d3c2920","2f7f8175-8e69-4670-ba26-a4676e19655b","56607e2e-1d2c-45cf-9ccf-e9e046a77ab4","52e62484-e9a4-4085-b32d-f1f6ede008fd","f1a5402b-7231-4c95-8982-2febde64d3fa","6512b310-0c0b-4f0b-a744-7820451b8f15","a87df9c6-a3b4-4606-8af1-a67d8e11bc8e","65aeeec8-430a-4e70-a191-891c22530531","b3019e7b-e09f-4ede-b8dc-aaa47275f3d8","3f3f48f4-4119-4151-9856-c088546467be","03d43c0d-c350-45f6-a690-dca7d82b35c3","fb55c4c3-2ba9-49dd-933f-c8d13eb3054f","1886a46f-d76a-4310-9623-d14bc5575783","bbae33d9-ba48-49d3-986f-e0b66db17678","9f079a42-b759-46fc-82ab-48e7b975a095"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785993952795057001,"uuid":"a4b2b310-0c5c-45e7-be2e-d0f61529c8ee"}